$DIR/test.p:14:27: cannot convert [5]byte{} (value of type [5]byte) to type Hdr
    This conversion is not allowed. T(x) converts between number types, between
    types with the same underlying type, and between pointers and
    unsafe.Pointer. It does not turn numbers into text: string(65) would make a
    rune, not "65".
    (see "Conversions" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.24)
    (run "pluto explain E0096" for a longer explanation)
